See [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) for the full picture. Quick rules for the frontend:

## Stack & layout

- Vue 3 with `<script setup>` Composition API; Inertia v2; Tailwind v4; Vite 6.
- Pages: `resources/js/Pages/`. Layout: `resources/js/Layouts/AppLayout.vue`.
- Components follow atomic design under `resources/js/Components/Spork/`:
  - `Atoms/` — basic building blocks (`SporkButton`, `SporkInput`, `SporkLabel`, `SporkTable`).
  - `Molecules/` — composed pieces (`Cards/`, `Containers/`, `Notifications/`).
  - `{Domain}/` — domain-specific (e.g. `Finance/`).
- Pass data through Inertia props from controllers — avoid extra `fetch()` calls when first-render data will do.
- Real-time: subscribe with Echo on private channels named `App.Models.{Model}.{id}`; on receipt prefer `router.reload({ only: [...] })` over manual mutation.

## Imports

```vue
<script setup>
import { ref, computed } from 'vue'
import { Head, Link, router, usePage } from '@inertiajs/vue3'
import AppLayout from '@/Layouts/AppLayout.vue'
</script>
```

## Spork UI styling

These tokens are load-bearing for dark mode and visual consistency.

### Palette

- Surfaces: `bg-white dark:bg-stone-800`, text `text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-200`, dividers `divide-stone-200 dark:divide-stone-600`.
- Primary action: `bg-indigo-500 dark:bg-indigo-600`. Destructive: `bg-red-500` / `text-red-500`. `slate` is reserved for focus chrome.
- Every color choice must include a `dark:` counterpart.

### Spacing

- Inline controls (buttons, dropdown rows): `px-3 py-2 text-sm`. Compact: `px-2 py-1 text-xs`. Headers/panels: `px-4 py-2`.
- Form fields, cards, modals: `p-4` bodies with `gap-4` or `gap-2` between stacked elements. Tables reserve `px-4 py-2` for top/bottom toolbars.
- Vertical rhythm uses Tailwind's even steps (`mt-2`, `mt-4`, `mb-4`). No arbitrary pixel values.

### Borders, corners, dividers

- Inputs / selects / textareas: `border border-stone-300 dark:border-stone-700` + `rounded-md`. Disabled: `bg-stone-200` or `dark:bg-slate-800/50`.
- Cards / tables / modals: `border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800` + `rounded-lg` + `shadow` / `shadow-sm`.
- Stacked rows: prefer `divide-y divide-stone-200 dark:divide-stone-600` over per-row borders.

### Focus & interaction

- Always `focus:outline-none` plus a Tailwind ring helper. Data-entry: `focus:ring-stone-500 focus:border-stone-500`. CTA buttons: `focus:ring-indigo-500 focus:ring-offset-2`.
- Hover should nudge background opacity, not swap colors drastically.

### Feedback

- Errors: `text-red-500 dark:text-red-400`, with `bg-red-100` when emphasis is needed.
- Selection / highlight pills: subtle neutral fills (`bg-stone-100 dark:bg-stone-700`) so they remain readable in tables and dropdowns.

## JS conventions

- Use `const` and `let`; no `var`.
- Prefer arrow functions and template literals.
- Destructure props and imports.
- Define props with `defineProps()`, emits with `defineEmits()`.
